  "verbalization": "Feigrisolide C is implicated in the regulation of Free fatty acid receptor 2 through multiple pathways, all of which converge on the A172 cell line. The evidence suggests that Feigrisolide C acts as a target for several compounds, including 3-O-beta-D-glucopyranosyl-oleanolic acid 28 O-beta-D-glucopyranoside, (3R,4R)-3-(1,3-benzodioxol-5-ylmethyl)-4-[(3,4-dihydroxyphenyl)methyl]oxolan-2-one, and 2-Acetoxytridecane, all of which are known to interact with Free fatty acid receptor 2. These interactions are supported by high scores in the integrated analysis, indicating a strong and consistent biological relationship. The mechanism likely involves the modulation of receptor activity, which could influence cellular processes related to lipid metabolism and signaling. The presence of multiple distinct compounds targeting the same receptor suggests a potential role in the regulation of fatty acid metabolism, possibly through the activation or inhibition of the receptor's signaling pathways. The integrated evidence supports a mechanistic link between Feigrisolide C and Free fatty acid receptor 2, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm the exact mode of action and therapeutic implications.",
